WEBVTT

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.870
You're lucky everything 
worked out for the best!

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.650
It was reckless of you 
to fly off like that.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.190
I'm sorry.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.120
As for the rest of you!

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.000
What would you have done if 
something happened to your pilot?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.070
I'm sorry, Boss.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.740
They acted under my authorization.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.410
Everyone, you've done well.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.970
Hurry back to the hospital 
and get some rest.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.330
All right.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.170
"Your Hero"

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.250
Nothing stands out as abnormal.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.010
You're free to return to your own room.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.490
But make sure to take it easy.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:05.930
Okay.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.230
Also, has Captain Suzukaze told you yet?

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.310
Ma'am?

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.160
She wants me to reexamine 
you in two or three days.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.230
More tests?

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.500
Just to play it safe.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.780
Okay...

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:21.740
Kei!

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:23.590
Are you all right?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.450
Uh, yeah... Thanks.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.320
Is there something on my face?

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.950
You've mellowed?

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.960
Thank goodness! You're 
back to your old self!

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:35.680
Officer Ange!

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.220
What was her problem?

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.310
Why don't we head on back?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.640
The doctor said I could 
return to my room.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.060
Great!

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.390
Why'd you bring him to my room?!

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:00.700
Hey, it's just for now.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.990
Izuru, act all cool! Act cool!

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.060
Cool!

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.340
Say, "I rock!" Say, "I rock!"

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:08.800
Huh?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:09.910
Say it while acting cool!

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.580
I rock.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.500
Hey! Quit messing with Izuru!

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.210
Why don't you go rest in your room?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.780
But it's more relaxing 
when I'm with everyone.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.710
I'll go back once!

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.450
What do you want?!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.480
Um, I wanted to offer 
a word of thanks...

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.490
Thank you very much for saving me.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.840
We should hold one after all.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.620
Ange needs a welcoming party!

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.410
A meeting between the GDF and 
the various economic powers?

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.720
Right. I will be accompanying the 
Commander in Chief to the meeting.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.330
Didn't anyone tell you?

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.710
No.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.980
I expect the AHSMB to be a 
major topic on the agenda...

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.530
Maybe they only informed 
Commander Simon.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.430
Could you switch to a private line?

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.680
Sure. Just a minute.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.350
What is it?

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.110
How much do you know 
about the AHSMB units?

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.350
In regard to...?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.270
The background behind their 
technological origins.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:22.420
Well, the brilliant scientist Juria 
Tsuda, who died at an early age,

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:25.680
developed technology that 
incorporated the pilot's DNA

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.530
into the central control system.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.090
How was Juria able to 
develop that technology?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.450
I don't know the specific details.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.880
So you don't know about how it 
came from a Wulgaru defector?

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.540
A Wulgaru defector?!

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.800
There was such a person? Who?

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.860
Is he still alive?

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.990
The defector is still alive...

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.260
...and currently under 
the MJP's custody.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.280
Why have you kept this a secret?

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.940
This person does not 
want an all-out war.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.940
Out of the desire to save us,

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.690
this person has only offered 
Wulgaru technology.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.280
Why are you sharing this with me?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.780
Albeit unofficially, Commander Simon

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.070
has already released some 
of this information.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.510
Aren't the AHSBM on the agenda 
in this upcoming meeting?

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.640
At the moment,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.450
only the Pacific Rim-Asia Alliance 
possesses AHSMB technology.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.340
I expect the other

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.710
economic powers to ask 
for AHSMB of their own.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.750
Is that a problem?

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.390
The JURIA-System that 
we have installed on the

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.790
AHSMB units is a dual-edged sword.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:23.270
Until the risks involved become clear,

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:25.230
we should postpone 
sharing that technology.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.730
Understood.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.980
I'll report in as soon 
as the meeting is over.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:29.970
Thank you.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.880
But this weighs heavy on me.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.890
Who is this Wulgaru defector?

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.310
For now, I've said all I can...

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.750
Thanks for waiting!

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.060
What gives?

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.500
What are those GDF dudes doing here?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.500
This looks good!

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.090
Tamaki, did you invite them?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.250
The more the merrier!

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.510
Yo!

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.490
We just returned to Star Rose ourselves.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.120
Guiliano told us that you were

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.150
throwing a welcoming 
party for a new recruit.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.180
Patrick was dying to come!

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.720
Sorry, but Ange might be a girl.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.640
Uh, actually, the one 
I wanted to see was...

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:18.950
Ciao!

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.900
Yep! It's great that the world 
is filled with all kinds of love.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.230
You've got it wrong!

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.270
Yo!

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.920
Officer Ange, these are 
our senior officers.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:31.530
They're Team Doberman.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.620
Nice to meet ya, Ange.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.370
The pleasure is all mine...

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:44.120
You've improved a lot!

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.850
Nah. I've still got a ways to go.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:48.390
So you still have a lot 
of room for improvement?

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.260
That's reassuring!

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.220
Izuru!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:52.900
Yes?

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.400
They need to reexamine you 
in two days at the hospital.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.750
It's just to play it safe.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:00.530
It doesn't hurt to have 
them look you over, right?

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:00.980
Yeah...

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.710
Officer Ange, why don't you come closer?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.490
This party is for you!

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.950
Uh, okay...

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.130
Ange!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:11.960
Yes?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.960
Ange, why does your personality change

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.680
when you pilot your AHSBM?

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.300
Do you realize that you act 
like a different person?

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.330
Y-you're wild and 
bursting with energy...

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.890
Yeah, you're just like an AK-47.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.300
You're powerful, but unpredictable 
when you cut loose.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.590
But you're tough, tenacious and simple,

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.210
making your highly reliable and durable!

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.010
I've been meaning to ask 
you about this as well.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.900
I'm not really sure why 
I change personalities,

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:38.600
but when I get inside of my AHSMB, 
it's like a different me surfaces...

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:42.490
I've heard of people acting 
differently when they drive,

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.300
but it's extreme in your case.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.400
Izuru acted a bit strange 
last time as well.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.160
Maybe it's because of how 
desperate the situation was?

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.570
But those situations seem to force 
the best results out of them.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.490
They were both incredible!

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.410
So we've got two ace pilots, huh?

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.120
Ange, you were great!

00:07:59.120 --> 00:07:59.830
So anyway-

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.690
What's the matter?
Does your stomach hurt?

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.270
Suruga, shut up!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.260
A bunch of things hurt.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.050
Asagi!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.540
What? It's just you.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.350
Couldn't you act a bit 
happier to see me?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.490
Out on errands?

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:23.740
Basically.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.770
I ordered some ice cream 
cones, so go pay for them.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.110
I have to pay?!

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:33.960
Here!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.090
Thank you.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.330
What's wrong with you?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.050
It's nothing.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.900
I'm willing to hear you out!

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.250
It's none of your business.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:46.970
She may have turned out down,

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:49.690
but time heals everything, 
so you'll be fine!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:50.710
Don't worry about it!

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.100
No one turned me down!

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.380
Then what's your problem?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.780
I realized that as a pilot, I'm 
nothing compared to those two.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:01.180
Jeez! That's all this is about?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.600
When did they get so far ahead of me...?

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:08.270
Asagi, you have plenty of good 
qualities that are yours alone!

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.730
Your face!

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.360
You really are King Considerate!

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.470
Hearing that from you doesn't 
make me the least bit happy.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.790
And am I seriously turning 
to a kid for moral support?

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:26.440
Officer Ange, you're fine.
 We'll handle the cleanup.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.130
No, I'll lend a hand.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.090
Asagi left sometime during 
the party, didn't he?

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.420
He might have gotten a tummy 
ache after eating too much.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.510
Why don't we drop by his room later?

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:37.430
Yeah.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.820
Master Daneel! Did you come to see me?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:43.990
Only in your dreams.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:47.100
Izuru, Daneel said that he'd 
like to have a word with you.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.020
What is it?

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.360
Lady Teoria said that she

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.780
wishes to dine with you 
if you are willing.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:56.680
For real?! As in a date?!

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.140
It is a dinner meeting.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.540
Then could I go with him?

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.330
Master Daneel, aren't you coming?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.080
Although I will be nearby, 
I will not dine with them.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.860
So they'll be alone? 
It really is a date!

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.660
Izuru's getting the jump on me!

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.630
Hey! You okay?

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.050
Nope. He froze.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:24.450
Why did you choose me?

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.270
You're here on behalf of Simon.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.050
Commander Simon isn't attending?

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.990
He isn't feeling well.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:33.500
I saw him just before 
I left to come here.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.890
He seemed well enough.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.360
There are a variety of 
political games at play.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.670
It's about to begin.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.270
Okay, let's begin the meeting!

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.340
What meeting?

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.700
Isn't that obvious?

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.110
The Izuru Date Battle Plan!

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:47.790
Date...

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:49.550
Aren't they just going out to eat?

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.210
Right! He'll be alone 
with his dream girl.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:53.630
Alone with her...

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.060
It might be a good idea 
to loosen up a bit.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:00.420
Roll your shoulders! Roll your neck!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.430
Uh, okay...

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.780
Listen, Izuru! Love 
is a game of politics!

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:07.420
You've gotta check out the girl's 
specs, imagine all possible scenarios,

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.440
devise a counter for each one 
and pick a plan of attack!

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.810
Ultimately, you gotta aim for 
her heart and hit it dead on!

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:14.480
Love struck!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:16.340
Since the Battle of Ceres,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.900
the Wulgaru have gradually 
been pushing the GDF back.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.040
If this war continues,

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.030
all we will do is lose 
more lives and money.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:27.380
We would hold peaceful 
negotiations if we could.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.300
Exactly! Our only option is to 
fight back with all we have.

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:33.220
We intend to increase our 
budget for defenses by 30%.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.040
We hope to help however we can.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.560
The same is true of us!

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:39.590
To meet those ends, we would like 
you to share your AHSMB technology.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.430
Unfortunately, the MJP's 
commander was unable

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.130
to attend this meeting 
due to health problems.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.110
The only way to fight on 
par with the Wulgaru is to

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:50.420
bolster the AHSMB team 
with all due haste!

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.830
We lack the time required 
to train new pilots.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.770
We would train them ourselves!

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.520
The AHSMB are still prototypes, 
so how about the Rhinos instead?

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:59.710
Isn't that the previous 
generation model?

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:03.110
Yes, but the Rhinos are already 
in line for mass production.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:07.030
Veteran pilots could rival our pilots 
within a short period of time.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.150
They can be used immediately

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:11.290
and are not as costly 
as the AHSMB units.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.460
They will have to do. We'll take them.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:17.380
Let's prepare to enter 
negotiations straightaway.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.100
You satisfied the other 
nations without handing

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.880
them the latest technology, and 
still managed to draw a profit.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:26.070
Now do you see the precocious 
position I am in?

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.390
I may lead the GDF,

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.740
but I am also the Minister 
of the Ministry of Defense

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:32.480
for the Pacific Rim-Asia Alliance.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.570
The Chinese and African economic powers

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:37.150
are lagging behind in space technology.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.840
They hope to do well in this

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.440
war so they can acquire 
new rights in outer space.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:44.170
Is this the time for 
such petty politics?

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.440
If we don't hand them everything

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:48.030
and form massive AHSMB fleets 
to oppose the enemy...!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.000
Assuming that was enough 
to defeat the Wulgaru,

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.630
what would be left when we won?

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:54.350
We would lose our standing 
as the world reproached us

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.790
for using genetically altered 
children in the war!

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.670
But only after they've 
stolen our technology.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:03.910
Somehow Bela-Russia has obtained 
the MJP's top-secret materials

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.760
and is currently producing 
mock AHSMB units.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.220
Everyone is only concerned with 
claiming rights over the resources in space, huh?

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.930
The United Organization of

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.850
American States is preparing 
to present a battleship.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.820
That's right. They plan on 
selling it during this meeting.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.770
It looks like they don't care 
to lose money or personnel.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.670
I feel horrible for those children.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.700
We're using them as chips in a 
political game so we can stay in control!

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:30.210
In other words, whether your 
date is a flop or not, Izuru,

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.050
rests on whether you have 
control of the situation!

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.290
Is that right?

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.390
Show a bit more interest!

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.260
Don't let her boss you around!

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.790
You've gotta make her 
march to the pace you set.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:42.590
Is Izuru capable of doing that?

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.880
We wouldn't be holding this 
meeting if I thought he could!

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:49.400
Yeah. This is my first time 
having dinner alone with a girl.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.830
But if we looked into 
each other's eyes,

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.610
couldn't we see into 
each other's hearts?

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:56.660
Huh? Wouldn't you wind 
up eating in silence?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.160
I'm fine with that...

00:13:58.160 --> 00:13:59.270
That's unacceptable!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.090
You two ladies!

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.050
Give Izuru some ideas on 
how to make a girl happy.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:04.670
Me!

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:05.510
You're up, Tamaki!

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:08.450
It'd make me happy if he 
fed me pickled fish guts!

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:10.570
But that only holds 
true for you, Tamaki.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:11.740
Then how about you, Kei?

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.980
Me...?

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:17.160
I'd like it if he seemed 
to enjoy the cake I baked.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.250
Pickled fish guts and home-made cake...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:19.910
Don't take notes!

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:23.170
And it'd be awesome if he 
put on this cool expression

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.930
while listening to me talk and 
complimented a whole bunch!

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:26.980
"You're right, Tamaki."

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:27.990
"You're adorable, Tamaki."

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:28.850
Like that!

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.600
I'd like it if he did little things

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.760
to show he cared and 
treated me kindly...

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.680
Don't turn Izuru into your ideal guy!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:36.990
Okay, I'll do my best!

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.640
Act cool while listening 
and complimenting her.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.780
And be kind while doing little 
things to show I care...

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:43.910
Dude, if you try to do all 
of that, you'll explode.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:46.060
Welcome back!

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.790
Where've you been?

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.820
Don't come in my room 
without permission!

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.170
You have impeccable timing, Asagi!

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.300
Man, accompany Izuru on his date.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:56.200
Why should I?

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:59.260
That may be the best suggestion 
I've heard so far!

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.250
I'd feel better if I had 
you there with me, Asagi.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.220
Yeah, that might be a good idea.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.940
If they're alone, Izuru 
might start to tense up.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.150
And I wouldn't have to worry 
if it was the three of you!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.590
Asagi, please.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.350
Is it time for your big date?

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:22.770
Asagi, Izuru! Commander 
Simon wants to see you.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.160
You did well in your last battle.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.070
Uh, sir!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.920
Izuru Hitachi, how are you feeling?

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.710
I heard that you underwent some exams.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:35.210
Sir, it's nothing...

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.840
I was told that I would need 
a reexamination, but I'm fine!

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.830
Toshikazu Asagi, how about you?

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.750
I... am fine.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.170
Regarding your futures.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.000
You have the option to leave

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.430
the battlefield and accept 
positions as instructors.

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:55.850
Sir, does this mean 
you are done with us?

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:00.310
I want to serve as an AHSMB pilot.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.450
Why is that?

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:04.970
The only reason I'm even 
getting to dine with Teoria

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.230
is because I'm here.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.150
And you?

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.880
If I have not been 
disqualified as a pilot,

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.340
I would like to continue 
piloting my AHSMB unit.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.080
That is what I have been trained to do.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:19.630
I cannot fathom a 
different path in life,

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.220
at least not right now.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.000
Very well.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.390
Ma'am, why did the commander ask that?

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:28.180
I'm not sure myself.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:30.810
You can't think about 
anything but that date, huh?

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:31.850
To be young!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.930
Well, I have to get ready!

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.830
Um, do you have a minute?

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.530
What's the matter?

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:41.580
Well, I imagine the commander must

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.580
have been worried about Izuru's health,

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.630
but in my case...

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.680
Did he ask about reassigning me

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.570
because I'm unfit to serve as a pilot?

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.120
That's not true.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:54.240
But I have the lowest Harmonic Levels...

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:57.480
And even as a pilot, compared 
to Izuru and Ange...

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.210
The "Fail 5".

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:03.860
Isn't that what you were 
called back at the academy?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.310
You had the aptitude,

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:08.950
but for some reason, none of you 
could live to your potential.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:09.680
Right...

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:12.420
Your major flaw is how you 
worry about everything.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:15.760
But that is also your strength.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:20.400
Your assignment is to evaluate 
yourself and then surpass yourself.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.390
Asagi!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.110
Great timing!

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:24.810
How so?

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.600
Our mission is finally about to begin!

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.120
You're bringing Asagi along?

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:35.250
He's my escort! Teoria 
gets to bring Daneel.

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:36.970
I plan on waiting outside.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:38.910
We're almost there.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:41.670
Where will they be eating?

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.020
At a restaurant that Teoria picked out.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.410
I wonder if it's a fancy restaurant.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:49.590
Do you hold the knife in your 
right hand or your left?

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.000
Hang in there!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.000
RED COMET
Okonomiyaki Teppanyaki Grill

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.010
OKONOMIYAKI

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:55.920
This it?

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.550
There is a private room in the back.

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:01.120
This is it!

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:07.390
Izuru, I'm glad you could make it.

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.490
Please take a seat.

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:10.620
Uh, okay!

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:13.620
I shall be waiting outside.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.360
If you need me for anything, 
please call for me.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:16.570
Same here.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:21.240
Asagi, if you like, you're 
welcome to join us.

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.880
The Wulgaru army is approaching the

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.750
perimeter of our absolute defense zone.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.010
They will clash with 
our army in 30 minutes.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.970
Don't create a pause in the bombardment!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.680
I don't care if the barrels burn out!

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:43.250
Anyone who falls so much as a step 
back will be shot on the spot!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:45.850
Make sure that we're constantly in 
front of the Bela-Russian fleet!

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.620
All ships, take off!

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:49.920
Show the Great Chinese Alliance

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.610
that Bela-Russia has 
developed its own fighters!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:07.290
No one ever mentioned going 
up against this massive army!

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:10.880
We have the Great Chinese 
Alliance, Bela-Russia

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:13.440
and the MJP's allied forces on our side.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.420
They probably aren't 
relaying their information.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.170
How can you be so calm?

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.750
We can't win if we can't work together!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.650
The MJP's reinforcements 
should be here momentarily.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:24.970
It'll all work out if we 
can survive that long.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.770
Damn! I can't ask the bunnies

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.930
to save our sorry hides all of the time!

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:32.180
That's right! This time, I'm 
going to protect Tamaki!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:34.860
Patrick, you look kinda different.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:36.500
"You judge a man by his looks"!

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.570
Randy, you're the one 
who always says that!

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.080
How are your preparations 
proceeding, Lumes?

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:47.750
According to plan.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:52.010
If you could draw the Earthlings' 
attention for a while longer,

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.370
we should be able to slip through 
their defenses with ease.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:56.480
What is it?

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.880
A squad is approaching from behind.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:02.230
Could they have perceived 
what our ulterior motive is?

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.940
No, this is...

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:05.000
Klein!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.190
Do you find this kind 
of restaurant agreeable?

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.620
Uh, yeah!

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:19.010
I had Daneel look for one where 
you would feel comfortable

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.590
so you wouldn't tense up.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.180
D-Daanel picked this place out?

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.660
"Daneel".

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:25.780
Uh, I'm sorry.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:30.040
Supposedly your manager 
recommended this restaurant.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.130
R-really?

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.000
It's about time I flipped this.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.110
I'm sorry!

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.690
I think it'll still taste the same.

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:45.520
Shut it!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:47.930
This is a rather unique dish, isn't it?

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:50.790
Not really. I just messed it up...

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:52.620
What goes in it?

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:55.100
Vegetables, wheat and... 
a bunch of stuff.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:56.880
Is that right?

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.400
I am always impressed by 
your culinary culture.

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:00.870
Impressed?

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:03.360
Did I use the word incorrectly?

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:05.280
No, you used it correctly.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.200
It was something I had never considered.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.510
Earthlings are a race 
rich in culture and you

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:14.710
possess various emotions referred 
to collectively as your "heart".

00:21:15.180 --> 00:21:17.570
I came with the intent to save you,

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:19.130
yet I have learned so 
much in the process.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:21.050
I am most grateful.

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.460
Same here!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.910
I'm only here because 
you came to our world.

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:30.030
I also learned the concept of 
"gratitude" after coming here.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:32.800
The same goes for taking others into 
consideration and worrying about others.

00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:36.810
In Wulgaru, everyone is only interested 
in their own desires and lusts.

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:41.870
Now I am filled with the wish 
to protect you and your kind.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:46.410
Teoria, I-I want to protect you, too!

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.450
Hot!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.400
Cool them down!

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.050
Are you okay?

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:52.300
Y-yeah...

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.240
I had you come here today

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:56.960
because I am concerned about something.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:58.850
You see...

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:02.430
Sorry to interrupt your meal!

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:04.300
You've been ordered to sortie!

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:08.390
The Wulgaru army has broken 
past our absolute defense zone!

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:56.040
"Defensive Battle at Cosmopolitan Academy
 (First Part)"
